Open local media selections without corrupting their bytes: browsers without
the File System Access API fall back to a FileReader upload, but the upstream
path always turns its buffer into a string-backed untitled editor. Media
previews need a readable binary resource, so retain media bytes in the existing
temporary filesystem and open that resource directly. Text files keep the
upstream untitled-editor behavior.

